---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { APP_ORIGIN } from "../lib/urls";

const title = "Not legal advice";
const description = "PMAP is not a law firm and does not give official legal advice.";
---

<SiteLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Not legal advice</h1>

  <p>
    Premarital Asset Protection is educational software. It does not create an attorney-client
    relationship, and no document it produces has legal effect until independent counsel redrafts it
    and it is signed with the formalities the governing forum requires.
  </p>

  <h2>Law differs by forum, sharply</h2>
  <p>
    Community property is not equitable distribution. Texas has limited statutory spousal
    maintenance, so "Texas has no alimony" is wrong. California requires seven calendar days between
    a final agreement being first presented and signed. Minnesota requires two witnesses and a
    notarial acknowledgment. New York requires acknowledgment in the form that would let a deed be
    recorded. Louisiana requires an authentic act. Nuptial agreements in England and Wales are not
    automatically binding. New Zealand applies relationship-property rules to many de facto couples.
  </p>

  <h2>Sole title is not a universal ownership rule</h2>
  <p>
    A deed, vehicle title, account registration, or company register can be important evidence, but the
    legal effect of sole title varies. Some systems classify property independently of whose name appears
    on title. Some impose special spouse-consent rules on a homestead or matrimonial home. Some permit
    broad disposition of genuinely separate property. Others give a family court power to adjust property
    or reverse dispositions despite title. <a href="/jurisdictions/">The jurisdiction matrix shows selected examples and primary sources.</a>
  </p>

  <h2>Cross-border cases need more than one answer</h2>
  <p>
    A couple can marry in one place, live in another, own real estate in a third, hold an entity in a fourth,
    and litigate in a fifth. The law governing an agreement, the law governing title to land, the forum's
    financial-relief powers, and the law governing a trust or entity can therefore be different. A transfer
    that is effective as a matter of title may still have consequences in the divorce forum, and a marital
    agreement valid where signed may not receive identical treatment elsewhere.
  </p>

  <h2>What we have checked, and what we have not</h2>
  <p>
    Every forum the product reaches has a jurisdiction pack, so none is silently missing. Roughly
    half cite a specific statute or case for their headline claims. The rest are marked
    <strong>unverified</strong> — they exist so the product does not pretend a place has no rules,
    and every unverified statement is flagged as a question for local counsel rather than an answer.
    The app shows you which of your forums are in which state, in the documents, before you read
    them. It also shows you the date the jurisdiction data was last reviewed. Law moves; that date
    tells you how much to trust what you are reading.
  </p>
  <p>
    The public <a href="/jurisdictions/">jurisdiction matrix</a> is a narrower, source-indexed subset. Its
    entries carry primary-source links and explicit review dates so they can be independently checked.
  </p>

  <h2>What is outside any agreement</h2>
  <p>
    Some things cannot be contracted at all — child support, custody, a retirement-plan survivor
    benefit waived before the wedding, an immigration affidavit of support.
    <a href="/limits/">Those limits are listed here</a>, and the app repeats them in the documents.
  </p>

  <h2>What this product does with aggressive planning</h2>
  <p>
    It may explain a jurisdiction's lawful mechanisms even when those mechanisms are unavailable elsewhere:
    separate-property tracing, partitions, exchanges, transmutations, changes of patrimonial regime,
    homestead analysis, domestic contracts, financial agreements, trusts, entities, and other structures.
    It does not convert a sham into a valid transaction. Fabricated gifts, secret return agreements,
    false disclosure, backdating, concealed beneficial ownership, and violations of injunctions or court
    orders are treated as different fact patterns, not clever versions of lawful planning.
  </p>

  <h2>What to do instead</h2>
  <p>
    Hire counsel licensed where you marry, where you will live, where a dispute may be heard, and where
    significant property is located — and let each party have their own. Use this product's output to
    arrive prepared with the classifications, source documents, jurisdiction questions, and proposed
    ownership terms already organized.
  </p>

  <p><a href={APP_ORIGIN}>Continue to the app</a> only if you understand the above.</p>
</SiteLayout>
